"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[4487],{13171:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"blogPosts":[{"id":"touying-0-8-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-8-0","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-09-15-touying-0-8-0.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-09-15-touying-0-8-0.md","title":"Touying 0.8.0","description":"Touying 0.8.0 is a big release, and the first that requires Typst 0.15. The headline feature is article mode: one source file compiles either to slides or to a flowing prose document. And we have two new animation functions.","date":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"September 15, 2026","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":3.055,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"},{"name":"Zralokh","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/zral0kh","imageURL":"https://github.com/zral0kh.png","key":"zral0kh"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-8-0","title":"Touying 0.8.0","authors":["orangex4","zral0kh"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.4","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-4"}},"content":"Touying 0.8.0 is a big release, and the first that requires **Typst 0.15**. The headline feature is **article mode**: one source file compiles either to slides or to a flowing prose document. And we have two new animation functions.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Article mode\\n\\nA handout deck written for projection rarely reads well as a prose document, and a document written for reading rarely projects well. Article mode lets one file be both. Compile with `--input export-mode=article` and the deck becomes a continuous document: no slide breaks, animations collapsed to their final state, images optionally floated to the side.\\n\\nThe interesting part is what happens where the two outputs should differ. `#article-text[..]` replaces the body of the slide it is written in, so a slide of bullet points can become a paragraph of prose:\\n\\n```typst\\n== Results\\n- First point\\n- Second point\\n\\n#article-text[\\n  In the article this slide becomes a prose paragraph instead of bullets.\\n]\\n```\\n\\n`#article-only[..]` and `#slides-only[..]` restrict content to one output, and `config-article(..)` covers the article side of the layout: `wrap` floats elements beside the text, `linearize` decides how much of the deck\'s structure comes apart \u2014 a composer\'s columns become flowing text, while a table with a header keeps its shape \u2014 and `#article-linearize[..]` / `#article-keep-layout[..]` override that per element. See [Article Mode](https://touying-typ.github.io/docs/integration/article-mode).\\n\\n## Two new animation functions\\n\\n`#animate` layers several effects on one piece of content, each over its own subslide range. A *placement* (`\\"show\\"`, `\\"cover\\"`, `\\"remove\\"` or `swap(..)`) decides whether the body appears; a styling function wraps whatever the placement left:\\n\\n```typst\\n#animate(\\n  [Photosynthesis],\\n  effects: (\\n    (effect: swap([Respiration], stretch: true), subslides: \\"2-\\"),\\n    (effect: (body, self: none) => text(fill: red, body), subslides: \\"3-\\"),\\n  ),\\n)\\n```\\n\\n`#touying-render` takes content held in a variable and renders it at a chosen stage, so an animated element can be shown mid-animation without writing it out again:\\n\\n```typst\\n#let steps = [A #pause B #pause C]\\n#touying-render(steps, subslides: 2)\\n```\\n\\n`#touying-recall` was extended from whole slides to any labelled element, and a `#slide[..]` can carry a label of its own, so several slides under one heading stay individually addressable.\\n\\n## Animations inside math\\n\\n`#pause`, `#uncover`, `#only` and `#alternatives` now work inside the math elements that keep their content in named fields \u2014 `frac`, `mat`, `vec`, `cases`, `binom`, `root`, `attach`, `accent` and the brace family. These used to abort the compile with `Unsupported mark`:\\n\\n```typst\\n$ frac(a #pause + b, c) $\\n```\\n\\n`touying-equation` is deprecated as a result; plain math is more capable than it ever was.\\n\\n## Things to watch when upgrading\\n\\n- **Typst 0.15 is required.**\\n- **A `#pause` after `uncover`/`only`/`alternatives` no longer skips the subslides they reserve.** v0.7.0 made a relative jump snap past any preceding wrapper, which was meant for `item-by-item` but caught the others too. If you relied on it, add the `#pause` yourself.\\n- **`show-bibliography-as-footnote` is a boolean now**, and `magic.bibliography()` is gone \u2014 set the flag and put a real `#bibliography(..)` in the presentation.\\n- **`semi-transparent-cover` is deprecated** in favour of `alpha-changing-cover` and `color-changing-cover`.\\n- **The speaker-note panel is a theme-supplied function** via `config-common(notes-fn: ..)`; the `config-methods(show-only-notes: ..)` renderer is gone.\\n\\nThe changelog has a full [migration guide](https://touying-typ.github.io/docs/changelog), and a separate one for theme authors at the end.\\n\\n## Also new\\n\\n- **`.pdfpc` files as bundle assets**, written directly instead of through a separate `typst query` step.\\n- **`touying-fn-wrapper-raw` parses and nests its body**, so `#alert[.. #pause ..]` works.\\n- **Overflow detection checks width as well as height**, and `detect-overflow` defaults to `auto`, following `breakable`.\\n- Internally, `src/core.typ` (6288 lines) was split into modules and the content handling was unified \u2014 most documentation pages were rewritten or corrected alongside it."},{"id":"touying-0-7-4","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-4","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-06-06-touying-0-7-4.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-06-06-touying-0-7-4.md","title":"Touying 0.7.4","description":"Touying 0.7.4 adds on-slide navigation arrows, easier integration with external packages, and a batch of fixes around warnings.","date":"2026-06-06T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"June 6, 2026","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":1.175,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"},{"name":"Zralokh","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/zral0kh","imageURL":"https://github.com/zral0kh.png","key":"zral0kh"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-7-4","title":"Touying 0.7.4","authors":["orangex4","zral0kh"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.8.0","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-8-0"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.3","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-3"}},"content":"Touying 0.7.4 adds on-slide navigation arrows, easier integration with external packages, and a batch of fixes around warnings.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n- **`lr-navigation`**: a navigation element with links to the previous and next subslide or slide, plus a centre icon ([#352](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/352)). Put it in a footer and the arrows become clickable links in the exported PDF; `mode` chooses between `\\"subslide\\"`, `\\"page\\"` and `\\"both\\"`, and `show-useless: false` hides links that would go nowhere. You can choose custom icons.\\n\\n```typst\\n#lr-navigation(mode: \\"both\\", show-useless: false)\\n```\\n\\n- **`touying-reduce`**: automatically looks up reducer bindings for a given package ([#363](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/363)), so integrating an external package\'s functions with Touying\'s animations takes less setup.\\n- **`components.full-width-block`**: a block that spans the full page width by cancelling the horizontal margins.\\n- **`lazy-layout`** gained a `grid-size` parameter for quantized position grouping, making column and row detection more robust.\\n- **Polish locale** for the outline message ([#372](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/372)).\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- *Minor breaking change*: the `lazy-layout` parameter of `cols` now defaults to `false` instead of `true`, so columns are no longer height-equalised unless you ask.\\n- `hide` no longer does unexpected things to headings ([#366](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/366)).\\n- `touying-fn-wrapper-raw` is now exported as part of the public API ([#362](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/362)).\\n- Mark warnings are improved and are also shown as `magic.warning` when `enable-mark-warning` is `false` ([#348](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/348)); a missing `fn` field in a mark warning message is handled gracefully.\\n- Warnings are now emitted via `uniwarn` ([#359](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/359))."},{"id":"touying-0-7-3","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-3","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-04-23-touying-0-7-3.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-04-23-touying-0-7-3.md","title":"Touying 0.7.3","description":"Touying 0.7.3 fixes a long-standing speaker-note pitfall \u2014 at the cost of two small breaking changes \u2014 and adds more control over item-by-item animations and progressive outlines.","date":"2026-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"April 23, 2026","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":0.99,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"},{"name":"Zralokh","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/zral0kh","imageURL":"https://github.com/zral0kh.png","key":"zral0kh"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-7-3","title":"Touying 0.7.3","authors":["orangex4","zral0kh"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.4","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-4"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.1","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-1"}},"content":"Touying 0.7.3 fixes a long-standing speaker-note pitfall \u2014 at the cost of two small breaking changes \u2014 and adds more control over item-by-item animations and progressive outlines.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Minor Breaking Changes\\n\\n**`#speaker-note[]` now always attaches to the slide above it** ([#354](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/354)), no matter how that slide was created: an explicit slide call, a heading-triggered section slide, or a normal content slide. This gets rid of the common pitfall where a `#speaker-note[]` placed after a slide silently created an unwanted empty \\"ghost\\" slide.\\n\\nAlong with it, `receive-body-for-new-section-slide-fn` and its variants now default to **`false`** (previously `true`). If you relied on content after a `= Section` heading being absorbed into the section slide body, set it explicitly:\\n\\n```typst\\n#import \\"@preview/touying:0.7.3\\": *\\n#import themes.university: *\\n\\n#show: university-theme.with(\\n  config-common(receive-body-for-new-section-slide-fn: true),\\n)\\n```\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n- **`item-by-item-fn`** and presets for it ([#347](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/347)).\\n- **Progressive outlines**: `custom-progressive-outline` was improved, and there is a new `section-relationship` ([#345](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/345)).\\n- **`cols`**: a new alias of `side-by-side`, with `cols` and the `lazy-*` components now exported ([#356](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/356)). `lazy-layout` also handles mixed layouts better ([#355](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/355)).\\n- **Metropolis** gained an outline slide ([#349](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/349)).\\n- A warning is now emitted when an empty slide content height is detected."},{"id":"touying-0-7-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-1","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-04-08-touying-0-7-1.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-04-08-touying-0-7-1.md","title":"Touying 0.7.1","description":"Touying 0.7.1 is a small follow-up release, focused on keeping content inside the slide it belongs to.","date":"2026-04-08T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"April 8, 2026","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":0.71,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"},{"name":"Zralokh","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/zral0kh","imageURL":"https://github.com/zral0kh.png","key":"zral0kh"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-7-1","title":"Touying 0.7.1","authors":["orangex4","zral0kh"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.3","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.0","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-0"}},"content":"Touying 0.7.1 is a small follow-up release, focused on keeping content inside the slide it belongs to.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n- **Overflow handling**: `breakable` and `clip` options to avoid slide overflow ([#336](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/336)). With `breakable: false` a slide is constrained to a single page instead of spilling onto a new one, and `clip` decides whether the excess is truncated or merely left to overhang.\\n- **`lazy-layout`**: new `lazy-v` and `lazy-h` components, plus `lazy-layout`, for equalising the heights of multiple columns (or the widths of multiple rows) ([#339](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/339)).\\n- **More title metadata**: `config-info` gained `contact` and `extra` fields ([#342](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/342)). `extra` takes a dict that a theme reads back as `self.info.extra.key`.\\n- **`touying-get-config`**: a function for reading the current configuration ([#333](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/333)).\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- `fit-to-height` and `size-to-pt` are fixed, and text is allowed to reflow ([#332](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/332)).\\n- Waypoint markers are fixed ([#341](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/341))."},{"id":"touying-0-7-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-0","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-03-30-touying-0-7-0.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-03-30-touying-0-7-0.md","title":"Touying 0.7.0","description":"Touying 0.7.0 is a large release built around one major feature \u2014 named waypoints \u2014 together with a long list of animation and layout fixes.","date":"2026-03-30T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"March 30, 2026","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":2.155,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"},{"name":"Zralokh","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/zral0kh","imageURL":"https://github.com/zral0kh.png","key":"zral0kh"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-7-0","title":"Touying 0.7.0","authors":["orangex4","zral0kh"],"tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.1","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.3","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-3"}},"content":"Touying 0.7.0 is a large release built around one major feature \u2014 **named waypoints** \u2014 together with a long list of animation and layout fixes.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Named waypoints\\n\\nAnimations have always been addressed by subslide number, which means counting `#pause`es by hand and renumbering everything whenever you insert one. Named waypoints ([#298](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/298), by [@zral0kh](https://github.com/zral0kh)) let you name a position in the animation instead.\\n\\n`#waypoint(<label>)` marks a spot \u2014 and, like `#pause`, advances to the next subslide unless you pass `advance: false`. A waypoint covers every subslide from its declaration until the next waypoint or the end of the slide, so passing the label to `uncover`, `only`, `effect` or `alternatives` shows content for exactly that stretch. Two markers turn a waypoint into an open range: `from-wp` is visible from it onwards, `until-wp` up to just before it. Labels need only be unique within a single slide, and they may be referenced before they are declared.\\n\\n```typst\\n#uncover(until-wp(<summary>))[Shown before the summary.]\\n\\nMain content.\\n\\n#waypoint(<summary>)\\n\\nSummary text. #pause More summary.\\n\\n#uncover(from-wp(<summary>))[Visible from the summary on.]\\n```\\n\\nThat is three subslides: the first shows the intro line and the main content, the second swaps it for the summary, the third adds the rest \u2014 and nothing had to be numbered. `get-first` and `get-last` pick out a single edge of a waypoint, `prev-wp` and `next-wp` shift a reference by whole waypoints, and hierarchical labels such as `<part:intro>` are combined when you refer to `<part>`. The `start` parameter sets where a waypoint begins independently of where it sits in the content ([#304](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/304)), and waypoints work in `handout-subslides` too.\\n\\n## Also new\\n\\n- **More flexible subslide numbers**: specifications now accept `auto` and the `\\"h\\"` (\\"here\\") string, with an inverse function for string subslide numbers and waypoints ([#301](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/301)).\\n- **Animation functions via reducer**: functions based on `fn-wrapper` are now implicitly allowed through the reducer ([#300](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/300)), making custom animation helpers easier to build.\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- **Covers**: `cover-with-rect` no longer breaks long lines of text when they are partially hidden, and colour and alpha covers gained fallback functions ([#328](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/328)). Cover spacing around lists was also fixed ([#303](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/303)).\\n- **Show rules**: ghost slides caused by show rules are gone, and show rules and the `defer` keyword are handled consistently ([#317](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/317)).\\n- **Headings**: `display-current-heading` uses explicit numbering when `style: auto` ([#329](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/329)).\\n- **Layout**: `alternatives-match` respects `stretch` ([#320](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/320)), and page margin merging and precedence are correct ([#322](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/322)).\\n- Plus `alert` no longer delayed ([#316](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/316)), negative subslide indices parsed correctly for `handout-subslides` ([#307](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/307)), and `slide` updating via a scoped import ([#310](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/310)).\\n\\nThanks for the contributions from [@zral0kh](https://github.com/zral0kh), [@Andrew15-5](https://github.com/Andrew15-5), [@navdeeprana](https://github.com/navdeeprana), and [@Cemoixerestre](https://github.com/Cemoixerestre)."},{"id":"touying-0-6-3","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-3","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-03-10-touying-0-6-3.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-03-10-touying-0-6-3.md","title":"Touying 0.6.3","description":"Touying 0.6.3 is a major bugfix release that also brings a batch of practical new features, most of them around animations and handout mode.","date":"2026-03-10T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"March 10, 2026","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":1.59,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-6-3","title":"Touying 0.6.3","authors":"orangex4","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.7.0","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-7-0"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.2","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-2"}},"content":"Touying 0.6.3 is a major bugfix release that also brings a batch of practical new features, most of them around animations and handout mode.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n- **`#jump` as unified animation control**: `#jump(n, relative: false)` is the new primitive for moving the subslide counter, and `#pause` and `#meanwhile` are now sugar on top of it. `#jump(3)` skips straight to subslide 3.\\n- **`#item-by-item`** reveals a list, enum or terms block one item at a time ([#278](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/278)):\\n\\n```typst\\n#item-by-item[\\n  - First\\n  - Second\\n  - Third\\n]\\n```\\n\\n- **`#touying-raw`** reveals a code block progressively, splitting on a `pause` comment in the code itself ([#283](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/283)):\\n\\n```typst\\n#touying-raw(```rust\\nfn main() {\\n    // pause\\n    println!(\\"Hello, world!\\");\\n}\\n```)\\n```\\n\\n- **Handout mode, more precisely**: `#handout-only[..]` marks inline content as handout-exclusive and the `<touying:handout>` label does the same for a whole slide ([#286](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/286)), while `handout-subslides` picks which subslides survive ([#288](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/288)).\\n- **Speaker notes and aspect ratios**: a full-screen notes mode with a slide thumbnail via `show-only-notes` ([#281](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/281)), and arbitrary aspect ratios such as 16-10 across all themes ([#280](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/280)).\\n- Also: a `subslide` parameter for `#touying-recall` ([#285](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/285)), `default-composer` in `config-common` for a global slide layout ([#284](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/284)), a `cover-fn` parameter on `uncover` for packages like Fletcher ([#267](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/267)), and inline minislides ([#228](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/228)).\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\nMany long-standing bugs are gone: ghost blank slides from a `touying-set-config` anchor regression, styled content on the first slide creating extra slides, `#meanwhile` being ignored inside grid cells and boxes, the `config:` parameter being silently ignored across all themes, and slides after `#show`/`#set` rules not rendering. See the [Changelog](/docs/changelog) for the full list.\\n\\n## For theme authors\\n\\nMove `config` to the **last** position in `utils.merge-dicts` so user overrides win, and replace `paper` with `utils.page-args-from-aspect-ratio` to support arbitrary aspect ratios:\\n\\n```typst\\nself = utils.merge-dicts(self, config-page(..utils.page-args-from-aspect-ratio(aspect-ratio), ...), config)\\n```\\n\\nThe documentation website was also substantially restructured in this release, with a new references page and docstrings across all source files."},{"id":"touying-0-6-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-2","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-03-06-touying-0-6-2.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-03-06-touying-0-6-2.md","title":"Touying 0.6.2","description":"Touying 0.6.2 is a small maintenance release, mostly about getting Touying working smoothly on Typst 0.14.","date":"2026-03-06T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"March 6, 2026","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":0.5,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-6-2","title":"Touying 0.6.2","authors":"orangex4","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.3","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.1","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-1"}},"content":"Touying 0.6.2 is a small maintenance release, mostly about getting Touying working smoothly on Typst 0.14.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n- **Typst 0.14 compatibility**: fixed `magic.bibliography-as-footnote` ([#249](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/249)) and the breakage of the `theorion` package on Typst 0.14.0 ([#237](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/237)).\\n- **Customisable checkerboard**: `components.checkerboard` now takes `columns`, `rows`, `alignment`, `primary` and `secondary` ([#161](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/161)).\\n- **Full-width headers**: ratio and relative margins are now supported ([#256](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/256)).\\n- **`#meanwhile` in CeTZ**: fixed ([#205](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/205)).\\n\\nPlus a handful of smaller fixes: the correct circle symbol, equation colour overrides via regex, `show-hide-set-list-marker-none` with a full enum, and better caching after removing the `dump` and `label-it` helpers."},{"id":"touying-0-6-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-1","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2025-01-01-touying-0-6-1.md","source":"@site/blog/2025-01-01-touying-0-6-1.md","title":"Touying 0.6.1","description":"Touying 0.6.1 adds first-class support for the theorion package and uses it as the default math theorem environment.","date":"2025-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"January 1, 2025","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":0.51,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-6-1","title":"Touying 0.6.1","authors":"orangex4","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.2","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.0","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-0"}},"content":"Touying 0.6.1 adds first-class support for the [theorion](https://github.com/OrangeX4/typst-theorion) package and uses it as the default math theorem environment.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n- **Theorion integration**: Added built-in support for the `theorion` package, which provides beautiful numbered theorem, lemma, corollary, definition, and proof environments. It is now the recommended way to write theorem blocks in Touying slides.\\n\\n```typst\\n#import \\"@preview/touying:0.6.1\\": *\\n#import themes.university: *\\n#import \\"@preview/theorion:0.3.2\\": *\\n#import cosmos.clouds: *\\n#show: show-theorion\\n\\n#show: university-theme.with(\\n  aspect-ratio: \\"16-9\\",\\n  config-common(frozen-counters: (theorem-counter,)),\\n)\\n\\n= Theorems\\n\\n== Prime numbers\\n\\n#theorem(title: \\"Euclid\\")[\\n  There are infinitely many primes.\\n]\\n```\\n\\nSee the [Theorion integration guide](/docs/integration/theorion) for more details."},{"id":"touying-0-6-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-0","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2024-12-01-touying-0-6-0.md","source":"@site/blog/2024-12-01-touying-0-6-0.md","title":"Touying 0.6.0","description":"Touying 0.6.0 is the first release since Typst 0.13 and brings several quality-of-life improvements.","date":"2024-12-01T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"December 1, 2024","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":0.655,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-6-0","title":"Touying 0.6.0","authors":"orangex4","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.1","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.5.0 \u2014 A Major Redesign","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-5-0"}},"content":"Touying 0.6.0 is the first release since Typst 0.13 and brings several quality-of-life improvements.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- **Auto heading style**: `utils.display-current-heading(level: 1, style: auto)` now respects show rules like `show heading: set text(blue)`.\\n- **Document metadata**: `config-info` fields are now applied to `set document` automatically.\\n- **`alternatives` default**: `stretch: false` is now the default \u2014 content no longer expands to fill the slide automatically. *(Minor breaking change \u2014 more intuitive behaviour.)*\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- Fix error with `uncover` using `semi-transparent-cover`.\\n- Fix type string comparison ([#153](https://github.com/touying-typ/touying/pull/153)).\\n- Fix horizontal-line bug in Typst 0.13.0.\\n- Refactor: fix `display-current-short-heading`.\\n\\n## Getting Started\\n\\n```typst\\n#import \\"@preview/touying:0.6.1\\": *\\n#import themes.university: *\\n\\n#show: university-theme.with(\\n  aspect-ratio: \\"16-9\\",\\n  config-info(\\n    title: [My Talk],\\n    author: [Alice],\\n    date: datetime.today(),\\n  ),\\n)\\n\\n#title-slide()\\n\\n= Introduction\\n\\n== Hello\\n\\n#lorem(40)\\n```"},{"id":"touying-0-5-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-5-0","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2024-09-01-touying-0-5-0.md","source":"@site/blog/2024-09-01-touying-0-5-0.md","title":"Touying 0.5.0 \u2014 A Major Redesign","description":"Touying 0.5.0 is a significant rewrite. The goal: make Touying more user-friendly, more flexible, and more powerful.","date":"2024-09-01T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"September 1, 2024","tags":[{"label":"release","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/release"}],"readingTime":0.76,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-5-0","title":"Touying 0.5.0 \u2014 A Major Redesign","authors":"orangex4","tags":["release"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.6.0","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-6-0"},"nextItem":{"title":"Touying 0.2.0","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-2-0"}},"content":"Touying 0.5.0 is a significant rewrite. The goal: make Touying more user-friendly, more flexible, and more powerful.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Major Changes\\n\\n### No more closures \u2014 cleaner config syntax\\n\\nConfiguration is now done with `config-xxx` functions:\\n\\n```typst\\n#show: university-theme.with(\\n  aspect-ratio: \\"16-9\\",\\n  config-colors(primary: blue),\\n  config-info(title: [My Talk], author: [Alice]),\\n)\\n```\\n\\n### New Stargazer theme\\n\\nA new visually striking theme, originally created by [Coekjan](https://github.com/Coekjan/) for the [touying-buaa](https://github.com/Coekjan/touying-buaa) project.\\n\\n### Fake frozen states\\n\\nUse numbering and `#pause` together without issues. Control with `config-common(frozen-counters: ...)`.\\n\\n### Special heading labels\\n\\n`<touying:hidden>`, `<touying:unnumbered>`, `<touying:unoutlined>`, `<touying:unbookmarked>` for precise control over heading behaviour.\\n\\n### `#show: appendix`\\n\\nFreeze the slide counter at the end of your main content:\\n\\n```typst\\n#show: appendix\\n\\n= Appendix\\n\\n== Extra Slide\\n\\nPlease pay attention to the current slide number.\\n```\\n\\n### Adaptive columns for outlines\\n\\n```typst\\n#components.adaptive-columns(outline(indent: 1em))\\n```\\n\\n## Migration Guide\\n\\nSee the [Changelog](/docs/changelog#v050) for the detailed step-by-step migration guide from 0.4.x."},{"id":"touying-0-2-0","metadata":{"permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-2-0","editUrl":"https://github.com/touying-typ/touying-typ.github.io/tree/main/blog/2024-01-17-touying-0-2-0.md","source":"@site/blog/2024-01-17-touying-0-2-0.md","title":"Touying 0.2.0","description":"Touying 0.2.0 is done.","date":"2024-01-17T00:00:00.000Z","formattedDate":"January 17, 2024","tags":[{"label":"development","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/tags/development"}],"readingTime":1.875,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"OrangeX4","title":"Maintainer of Touying.","url":"https://github.com/OrangeX4","imageURL":"https://orangex4.cool/images/icons/profile.jpg","key":"orangex4"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"touying-0-2-0","title":"Touying 0.2.0","authors":"orangex4","tags":["development"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Touying 0.5.0 \u2014 A Major Redesign","permalink":"/touying/latest/blog/touying-0-5-0"}},"content":"Touying 0.2.0 is done.\\n\\n## Implemented Features\\n\\n- [x] **Object-oriented programming:** Singleton `s`, binding methods `utils.methods(s)` and `(self: obj, ..) => {..}` methods.\\n- [x] **Page arguments management:** Instead of using `#set page(..)`, you should use `self.page-args` to retrieve or set page parameters, thereby avoiding unnecessary creation of new pages.\\n- [x] **`#pause` for sequence content:** You can use #pause at the outermost level of a slide, including inline and list.\\n- [x] **`#pause` for layout functions:** You can use the `composer` parameter to add yourself layout function like `utils.side-by-side`, and simply use multiple pos parameters like `#slide[..][..]`.\\n- [x] **`#meanwhile` for synchronous display:** Provide a `#meanwhile` for resetting subslides counter.\\n- [x] **`#pause` and `#meanwhile` for math equation:** Provide a `#touying-equation(\\"x + y pause + z\\")` for math equation animations.\\n- [x] **Slides:** Create simple slides using standard headings.\\n- [x] **Callback-style `uncover`, `only` and `alternatives`:** Based on the concise syntax provided by Polylux, allow precise control of the timing for displaying content.\\n  - You should manually control the number of subslides using the `repeat` parameter.\\n- [x] **Transparent cover:** Enable transparent cover using oop syntax like `#let s = (s.methods.enable-transparent-cover)(self: s)`.\\n- [x] **Handout mode:** enable handout mode by `#let s = (s.methods.enable-handout-mode)(self: s)`.\\n- [x] **Fit-to-width and fit-to-height:** Fit-to-width for title in header and fit-to-height for image.\\n  - `utils.fit-to-width(grow: true, shrink: true, width, body)`\\n  - `utils.fit-to-height(width: none, prescale-width: none, grow: true, shrink: true, height, body)`\\n- [x] **Slides counter:** `states.slide-counter.display() + \\" / \\" + states.last-slide-number` and `states.touying-progress(ratio => ..)`.\\n- [x] **Appendix:** Freeze the `last-slide-number` to prevent the slide number from increasing further.\\n- [x] **Sections:** Touying\'s built-in section support can be used to display the current section title and show progress.\\n  - [x] `section` and `subsection` parameter in `#slide` to register a new section or subsection.\\n  - [x] `states.current-section-title` to get the current section.\\n  - [x] `states.touying-outline` or `s.methods.touying-outline` to display a outline of sections.\\n  - [x] `states.touying-final-sections(sections => ..)` for custom outline display.\\n  - [x] `states.touying-progress-with-sections((current-sections: .., final-sections: .., current-slide-number: .., last-slide-number: ..) => ..)` for powerful progress display.\\n- [x] **Navigation bar**: Navigation bar like [here](https://github.com/zbowang/BeamerTheme) by `states.touying-progress-with-sections(..)`, in `dewdrop` theme.\\n- [x] **Pdfpc:** pdfpc support and export `.pdfpc` file without external tool by `typst query` command simply."}]}')}}]);